  "findings": [
    {
      "finding": "Registry/executor correctly define UC Persona as no API key with durable Clerk credentials, but provider catalog groups all web-cookie providers as toggleAuthType=apikey and no UC-specific email-login modal exists. The generic modal therefore presents an API-key/cookie-style add flow.",
      "id": "UC-AUTH-UI-01",
      "severity": "blocking"
    },
    {
      "finding": "UC emailLogin.ts is fully implemented and offline-tested but has no production caller. POST /api/providers/[id]/login only dispatches MaxAI, Adobe, Conol, then generic browser login; it never dispatches UC request/verify steps.",
      "id": "UC-AUTH-API-01",
      "severity": "blocking"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Canonical provider is uc-persona with uc/ucn aliases, but WEB_SESSION_CREDENTIAL_REQUIREMENTS is keyed only as uc. uc-persona therefore has no web-session requirement. Generic connection POST also hardcodes authType=apikey.",
      "id": "UC-AUTH-CANON-01",
      "severity": "blocking"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Personal Codex/Gmail helper only retrieves and prints an OTP in --test-fetch-only mode. It does not request a code, call OmniRoute login request/verify endpoints, or persist credentials. It is not integrated with portal/UI.",
      "id": "UC-AUTH-PERSONAL-01",
      "severity": "blocking"
    },
    {
      "finding": "UC Direct is correctly modeled as a separate metered X-API-Key surface and has no configured connection, but it remains registered/routing-capable in code. The audit-required policy-disabled/ineligible state is documented intent, not enforced by an explicit product gate.",
      "id": "UC-DIRECT-01",
      "severity": "policy-gap"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Live/local/next/candidate all contain identical 19-model static Persona catalog. Dynamic upstream Persona roster discovery remains optional and not implemented.",
      "id": "UC-MODELS-01",
      "severity": "ready-static"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Existing active Persona connection remains provider=uc and auth_type=apikey despite containing the correct Clerk providerSpecificData. Aliases let routing work, but portal metadata remains misleading until transactional canonical migration to uc-persona/cookie or dedicated auth type.",
      "id": "UC-DB-01",
      "severity": "migration-needed"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Before release, add an explicit negative policy gate proving UC Direct cannot be onboarded, credentialed, routed, or used as fallback. Merely having zero current connections is insufficient.",
      "id": "UC-DIRECT-POLICY-02",
      "severity": "blocking-policy"
    }
  ],
